</directives>

§ Context
# Goal
Resolve the two major architectural pain points identified in the Sovereign/Tau monorepo:
1. Fix the "hidden uu" & quoting/brokenness in the in-process shell builtins (`crates/pi-builtins` and `crates/pi-shell`).
2. Reconcile the monorepo split-brain between root `/home/toxic/estate` and `/home/toxic/estate/projects/tau` (aliased as `engine`) so that `engine` can be eliminated cleanly without destroying Sovereign control-plane assets.

# Findings & Ground Truth
- The user is running within the TUI (Tau/OMP).
- In-process builtins live in `crates/pi-builtins` (Rust crate based on uutils/brush-builtins, embedded via `pi-natives` / `pi-shell`).
- The builtins (`rg`, `grep`, `find`, `fd`) are "hella broken" when users run commands with "hidden uu" flags (e.g. `rg --hidden`, `rg -u`, `rg -uu`, `fd -H`, etc.) or encounter quote-parsing edge cases.
- CRITICAL WARNING FOR BUILTINS: When running in-process, `std::env::args()` returns the parent CLI process (`tau` / `omp`), NOT the builtin's CLI invocation arguments! Arguments to builtins are passed into the `Utility::run` or Clap struct.
- MONOREPO SITUATION: Root `/home/toxic/estate` holds the Sovereign control plane (Go inference `herd`, Python daemons, Svelte apps, skills in `skills/` and `skills/managed/`). `projects/tau` is the Tau coding-agent monorepo (`packages/ai`, `packages/catalog`, `packages/coding-agent`, etc.). `engine` was a symlink to `projects/tau`.
